# A method call is linked again when a receiver it has seen gets the method later: the function that stores the method on the receiver and gives the receiver a prototype with the method is reached only through this call, and both methods are linked in the end, no method of an object outside the chain
# RUN: flow-links calls
# CHECK: [[caller]] f0 v9 -> [[first]] f1 Call Once
# CHECK: [[caller]] f0 v9 -> [[own]] f2 Call Once
# RUN(INHERITED): flow-links calls
# INHERITED: [[caller]] f0 v9 -> [[first]] f1 Call Once
# INHERITED: [[caller]] f0 v9 -> [[inherited]] f3 Call Once
# RUN(NOWHERE): flow-links calls
# NOWHERE-NOT: -> {{*}} f4
# RUN(STARTER): flow-solve nodes
# STARTER: , f0, v3) = {L3#[[starter]]}
# STARTER: , f1, parameter 0) = {L3#[[starter]]}
# RUN(OWN): flow-solve nodes
# OWN: , f0, v1) = {L0#[[receiver]]}
# OWN: , f2, parameter 0) = {L0#[[receiver]]}
# RUN(PARENT): flow-solve nodes
# PARENT: , f0, v1) = {L0#[[receiver]]}
# PARENT: , f3, parameter 0) = {L0#[[receiver]]}

